/** * Listener interface for item template creation events. *
* Mods implementing this interface will be notified when Wurm's item templates * have been loaded from the database and are ready for use or modification. * This is the ideal time to create custom items using @link com.garward.wurmmodloader.modsupport.ItemTemplateBuilder. * *
* Use this listener when you need to: * *
Create custom item templates *
Modify existing item templates *
Access or validate item template data *
Register items that depend on existing templates * * *
* Example usage: * @code * public class MyMod implements WurmServerMod, ItemTemplatesCreatedListener { * @Override * public void onItemTemplatesCreated() { * ItemTemplateBuilder builder = new ItemTemplateBuilder("mymod.custom.item"); * builder.name("Custom Item", "custom items", "A custom item"); * builder.weightGrams(1000); * builder.build(); * } * } * @endcode * *
* Lifecycle order: * *
@link WurmServerMod#preInit() *
@link WurmServerMod#init() *
@link #onItemTemplatesCreated() ← You are here *
@link ServerStartedListener#onServerStarted() * * * * @see com.garward.wurmmodloader.modsupport.ItemTemplateBuilder * @see WurmServerMod * @since 1.0.0 */
